---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PAGES } from '../../data/beatles.mjs';

const talk = PAGES.slice(1);
---
<Base title="Learn" description="The tutorial, the Beatles Bench talk as pages, and how to test ThinkThen before you trust it.">
  <h1>Learn</h1>
  <p class="lede">Start with the tutorial. Then watch ThinkThen work on Beatles songs, where every answer is known.</p>

  <div class="grid">
    <a class="tile" href="/learn/tutorial/"><b>Tutorial</b><span>From the install line to a pipeline that sorts a stream of messages.</span></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/learn/beatles-bench/"><b>Beatles Bench</b><span>The talk as {talk.length} short pages. Each shows one slide, one command, and what a different bar changes.</span></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/trust/"><b>Test it before you trust it</b><span>Outcomes, thresholds, saved answers, and checking a question against your own records.</span></a>
  </div>

  <h2>Beatles Bench</h2>
  <ol class="talk">
    {talk.map((p) => <li><a href={p.route}>{p.command ? <><code>{p.title.split(' ')[0]}</code> {p.title.split(' ').slice(1).join(' ')}</> : p.title}</a></li>)}
  </ol>

  <h2>Reference</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/reference/">reference</a> lists every flag, exit code, and output field. <a href="/refusals/">What it will not do</a> lists every line the tool will not cross.</p>
</Base>
